 "standard_code": "Grade 8: 1.3 Exponents",
 "standard_url": "https://www.education.gov.za/Portals/0/CD/National%20Curriculum%20Statements%20and%20Vocational/CAPS%20SP%20%20MATHEMATICS%20GR%207-9.pdf",
 "standard_text": "Compare and represent integers in exponential form; compare and represent numbers in scientific notation; extend the general laws of exponents to include: a^m × a^n = a^(m+n), a^m ÷ a^n = a^(m−n) if m > n, (a^m)^n = a^(m×n), (a × t)^n = a^n × t^n, a^0 = 1.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 8 exponents worksheets: multiplying and dividing powers, power of a power, zero exponents and laws with letters. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "Multiply: add the exponents.",
 "key_sub": "a⁰ = 1.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li>Multiply powers with the same base: add the exponents. 2³ × 2⁴ = 2⁷.</li><li>Divide: subtract the exponents. 5⁶ ÷ 5² = 5⁴.</li><li>Power of a power: multiply the exponents. (3²)³ = 3⁶.</li><li>Any number (not 0) to the power 0 is 1: 7⁰ = 1.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>x⁵ × x³ ÷ x²</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>x⁸ ÷ x²</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: x⁶</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Multiplying the exponents</td><td>When multiplying powers, add them.</td></tr><tr><td>Multiplying the bases</td><td>2³ × 2⁴ = 2⁷, not 4⁷.</td></tr><tr><td>a⁰ = 0</td><td>a⁰ = 1.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does CAPS Grade 8 say about exponents?",
   "a": "Use the laws of exponents: multiplying and dividing powers with the same base, a power of a power, and the zero exponent."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is 10⁰?",
   "a": "1."
  },
  {
   "q": "Is 2³ × 3² = 6⁵?",
   "a": "No: the bases are different."
  },
  {
   "q": "What is (2x)³?",
   "a": "8x³."
  }
